

⭐ 1. FULL “GETTING STARTED” TUTORIAL

A complete onboarding flow for a new user.

Step 1 — Install Python & Dependencies

pip install numpy cryptography matplotlib

Step 2 — Create a Scenario File

Save this as scenarios/my_first_run.json:

{
  "author": "C. MATTHEW BLACKWELL — Independent Designer",
  "scenario_name": "first_test",
  "duration_seconds": 5.0,
  "dt_seconds": 0.01,

  "materials": {
    "alloy_x": {
      "max_temp": 1200,
      "yield_strength": 450000000,
      "fatigue_limit": 0.85
    }
  },

  "geometry": {
    "wall": {
      "material": "alloy_x",
      "volume_m3": 0.1,
      "surface_area_m2": 1.0
    }
  },

  "power_systems": {
    "coil": {
      "max_draw_watts": 3000,
      "efficiency": 0.9
    }
  },

  "plasma_regions": {
    "zone_1": {
      "initial_density": 1e19,
      "initial_temperature": 100000,
      "stability_threshold": 0.7
    }
  },

  "environment": {
    "pressure_pascals": 0.0001,
    "min_pressure_allowed": 0.00001
  },

  "constraints": {
    "max_temp": { "wall": 1100 },
    "max_stress": { "wall": 400000000 },
    "max_fatigue": { "wall": 0.8 },
    "max_power_draw": { "coil": 2800 },
    "plasma_stability_threshold": 0.7,
    "min_pressure": 0.00001
  }
}

Step 3 — Run the Simulation

python cli/main.py simulate --config scenarios/my_first_run.json

Step 4 — Validate the Run

python cli/main.py validate-run --input sealed_record.json

Step 5 — Export a Report

python cli/main.py export-report --input sealed_record.json

